n was critical in consolidating and maintaining his kin-group's dominance over the fertile lands of Munster. His rule represents a period of entrenchment for the Eóganachta, a dynasty that would exert profound influence over southern Ireland for centuries, tracing its lineage through figures like his great-grandfather, Feidlimid mac Óengusa, a previous king.

